Unsupervised learning, on the other hand, involves training an algorithm on an unlabeled dataset, where the correct answers are not known. The algorithm must identify patterns and relationships in the data on its own, without any guidance. For example, an unsupervised learning algorithm could be used to cluster customer data based on purchasing habits, without any prior knowledge of what those habits might be.
